-- The schema as it stands, and the first migration Drizzle owns.
--
-- Seventeen hand-written files made this schema, one ticket at a time. They are not
-- replayed here: this is `pg_dump --schema-only` of the database they produced, verified
-- object-for-object against it, so what a fresh clone builds is exactly what the Cluster
-- already runs. Their reasoning is not lost — it is in `docs/adr/`, in `CONTEXT.md`, and
-- in the `comment on` statements below, which is where a reader looks anyway.
--
-- **It is a dump and not a generated file on purpose.** `drizzle-kit pull` was tried first
-- and is lossy against this schema: it scrambles composite index column order, drops `desc`
-- and `nulls last`, drops `nulls not distinct` — which is an invariant, not a hint — and
-- models neither the trigger function below nor its two triggers. See ADR-0009.
--
-- Everything after this file is generated by `drizzle-kit generate` from `db/schema.ts`,
-- except what Drizzle cannot express: the function and triggers are hand-written SQL here
-- and will be hand-written SQL in any migration that changes them.

